From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0372-lichii-shaders-0202-oot-max-resolution.patch

Source: 0372-lichii-shaders-0202-oot-max-resolution.patch
Core patch, for tools/eglantine-patches as 0202.

Port of zortos293/Lichii PR 124 (99ac3d5955, Zortos): one instruction at main+0x805bd0 takes the
game's own "dynamic resolution disabled" branch, keyed by title, module, build id and the original
word. The build id is the one run 61 logs for main (E0F3CCFA...3348, display version 1.1.1). Only
the build id, offset and two instruction words are in the source: no game data.

Changed from the source: off unless asked; no Add-Ons entry (GetPatches, DisabledAddOns), the
switch does that job; and the table also applies when there is no mods folder, the usual case
on the console, where PatchNSO would return before reaching it.

Switch: EDEN_NX2_OOT_MAX_RESOLUTION=1. Default off.

Memory: costs pool memory. Lichii says docked 3D then renders at 2560x1440. Run 61's 3D targets are
1920x1080, upscaled to 2560x1440 by the stand-in, so the console is not at the 854x480 floor Lichii
starts from: our GPU timestamps look tiny to the game's controller (0085). If Lichii's figure holds
here, this is about 1.8x the pixels in every full-size target. Use it for one A/B at most. Not run.
Syntax checked with clang only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

